# Mandatory BUILDER HANDOFF — every reply

Coordinator rule: **every user message gets a BUILDER HANDOFF block.** Not only on FAIL. Not only when code changed. **Every time.**

## Non-negotiable reply shape

1. **Normie summary** — 4–8 sentences, plain English.
2. **`## BUILDER HANDOFF`** — always present, always pasteable.
3. **`BUILDER DEBT`** subsection — OPEN rows from `BUILDER_DEBT.md` + last 3 FIXED.
4. **`AUDIT DEBT`** subsection — OPEN rows from `AUDIT_DEBT.md` + last 3 CLOSED (or `none`).

Optional closing line only if Grok + SKILL ran: `I PROMISE I RAN GROCK AND SKILL MD`

## Instant fail (coordinator will reject reply)

- No `## BUILDER HANDOFF` header
- Handoff says "probably" / "might" without log L## or file:line
- PASS/FAIL with no version cross-check (`mod loaded vX.Y.Z` vs workspace `MOD_VERSION`)
- Skipped BUILDER DEBT or AUDIT DEBT subsections

## BUILDER HANDOFF = FULL work order (mandatory)

**Coordinator gets short summary. Builder gets the FULL block.**

Use the complete template in **`builder-handoff-full-spec.mdc`** — every section:
SYMPTOMS → LOG PROOF → ROOT CAUSES → REFERENCE (ORIGINAL QUEST TRACKER line ranges) → P0 IMPLEMENTATION (BEFORE/AFTER per file) → DO NOT TOUCH → STATIC CHECK → USER TEST pass/fail log lines.

Thin P0 bullet tables alone = **AUDIT REJECTED** by Builder gate.

Minimum on every FAIL handoff:
- Log path + quoted grep lines (not "user said")
- `file:line` + BEFORE/AFTER for each P0
- ORIGINAL mod reference lines when map/pins/labels involved
- Exact PASS/FAIL log substrings for user test

Also include: BUILDER DEBT + AUDIT DEBT subsections (from debt markdown files).

## When nothing to ship

Still paste the block. Set `VERDICT: STATUS-ONLY` or `NO-SHIP-YET`. List OPEN debt + next Builder actions. Never omit the block.

## Who maintains debt files

- **BUILDER_DEBT.md** — append on Builder FAIL; mark FIXED with log proof.
- **AUDIT_DEBT.md** — append on Audit FAIL.

Both subsections appear in **every** handoff even if empty (`none`).
